  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of Member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Kenya ratified, in consultation with social partners the 2014 Protocol to ILO Convention 29 on Forced Labor, Convention 181 (Private Employment Agencies), Convention 189 (Domestic Workers) and Convention 150 (Labor Administration). Through USA, Department of Labor, Bureau for International Labor Affairs funded projects; All Hands in Kenya: Advancing Labour Standards through Cooperative Action&#x201d; [KEN/20/01/USA] and Strengthening Capacity of Governments to Address Child Labour and Forced Labour, Violations of Acceptable Conditions of Work&#x201d; [RAF/19/09/USA], ILO is supporting the government and constituents in Kenya in strengthening the capacity to ratify a number ILO conventions; 29, 181, 189 and 150.  In view of this the ILO initiated technical consultations with constituents which led to the convening of a technical meeting in July 2023 to discuss such conventions, and agree on a gap analysis on un-ratified ILO conventions for Kenya</narrative>
   </description>
